            <ArticleTitle>[Effect of impulse-sensory training on peripheral blood indicators].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>105-10</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Hematological studies of 93 patients with coronary heart disease (the main group comprised 35 subjects and 4 control groups 58 subjects) and mathematic analysis of the data obtained have demonstrated that application of impulse and sensory training leads to a number of significant alterations on the part of the peripheral blood, with these alterations being similar to those seen during the performance of physical work or mental ideas associated with this work performance.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
